            <ArticleTitle>Retrograde approach to a totally occluded right coronary artery via a septal perforator artery: the tale of a long and winding wire.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E65-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Retrograde recannalization of chronic total occlusions has developed as a viable alternative to restore coronary patency. Techniques continue to evolve and complications described. We present a new complication related to equipment developed to improve outcomes via a retrograde approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
